WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.202 --> 00:00:03.785
(upbeat music)

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.240
- In vitro fertilization is a process

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:29.470
where a woman's eggs are
fertilized outside her body

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:33.033
then placed back inside her
body to help her get pregnant.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:39.613
A woman's reproductive
system includes the vagina,

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.253
cervix,

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.573
uterus,

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.693
fallopian tubes,

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.530
and ovaries.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.020
During the monthly menstrual cycle,

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.730
one of the ovaries releases an egg

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:02.913
in a process called ovulation.

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:08.893
After ovulation, the egg
enters the fallopian tube.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:13.950
A woman is most likely to
become pregnant if she has sex

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:18.473
in the days just before, during,
or right after ovulation.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.330
During this time a sperm cell

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:25.100
from a man's reproductive
fluid, called semen,

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.873
is able to fertilize the egg
just inside the fallopian tube.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:34.580
As it travels along the fallopian tube

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:37.200
the fertilized egg now called an embryo

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.393
loses the outer cells that
nourished it in the ovary.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.023
The embryo passes from the
fallopian tube into the uterus.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:52.030
In the uterus the embryo sheds
its protective outer layer,

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.650
called the zona pellucida,

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:55.993
in a process called zona hatching.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.590
Zona hatching is necessary
for the embryo to implant

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:02.733
in the tissue lining the uterus.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.640
During implantation a
connection between the woman

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.533
and the embryo begins to grow.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.000
This organ, called the placenta,

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.893
allows oxygen and nutrients to
pass from her to the embryo.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:21.090
In vitro fertilization may be performed

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.650
if a woman has been having
trouble getting pregnant,

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.140
a condition known as infertility,

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:28.730
or it may be done if a
woman wants to have a child

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.183
without a male partner.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:37.270
Before in vitro fertilization
a woman will receive

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:40.790
fertility medication that
causes more than one egg to grow

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:42.643
and mature in the ovaries.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.150
A man will provide a semen sample

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:48.570
so that the healthiest
sperm can be collected

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.963
for fertilization.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:53.360
If the male partner is
completely infertile,

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:54.830
also known as sterile,

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:56.890
or the woman doesn't have a male partner,

00:02:56.890 --> 00:03:00.323
a donor may be arranged to
provide sperm for this process.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.910
In vitro fertilization consists
of three main procedures,

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.563
follicle aspiration,

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:13.973
fertilization,

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:17.163
and embryo transfer.

00:03:20.281 --> 00:03:23.400
During the first procedure,
called follicle aspiration,

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.803
eggs will be harvested from the ovaries.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:29.900
At the beginning of this procedure

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:33.240
an ultrasound probe will be
inserted into the woman's vagina

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.643
so that her doctor can view her ovaries.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.840
Inside the ovaries the doctor
will look for follicles.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:45.623
Each follicle is a fluid filled
sack that contains an egg.

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:50.670
Then the doctor will
insert a long thin needle

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:53.000
into and through the wall of her vagina,

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.590
and guide it to the ovary.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.910
A suction device connected to the needle

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.943
will collect several eggs
from inside their follicles.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:07.440
During the second part of
in vitro fertilization,

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.490
called fertilization,

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:11.580
the collected eggs will
be taken immediately

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.233
to a laboratory where
they will be fertilized.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:20.560
Fertilization may be
performed by insemination

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.653
where several sperm are mixed
with the healthiest eggs,

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:29.040
or the eggs may be fertilized
with sperm injected

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.640
directly into them during a process called

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.173
intracytoplasmic sperm injection.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:38.350
The fertilized eggs, also called embryos,

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:40.700
will be monitored for three to five days

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.113
as they begin to grow.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.960
At this time the lab may create
a hole in the zona pellucida

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.980
surrounding some of the embryos.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:51.530
This process, called assisted hatching,

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:54.333
will help these embryos
implant in the uterus.

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:57.730
Some of the embryos
will be used right away

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.223
for embryo transfer,

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:03.530
and the rest will be frozen
and stored for future use

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:04.713
if necessary.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:09.670
The third part of in vitro fertilization

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:11.840
is called embryo transfer,

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:15.930
which is done three to five
days after fertilization.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:17.480
During embryo transfer,

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:19.760
a tool called a speculum will be inserted

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:22.350
into the woman's vagina
so that the doctor can see

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:23.423
her cervix.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.140
A syringe will be loaded
with fluid containing one

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:29.640
or more of the hatched embryos.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.720
Then the syringe will be
attached to a long thin tube

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:33.883
called a catheter.

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:39.100
The doctor will insert the
catheter into the vagina

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:43.493
through the cervix and into the uterus.

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:49.693
Once inside the uterus, the
doctor will inject the embryos.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:55.023
Then the catheter and
speculum will be removed.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:00.010
The woman may continue to lie on her back

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:01.893
for about 15 minutes.

